<!--
  The status-bar notification icon.

  **Must be a flat, single-colour silhouette on transparency.** Android >= 5.0 discards every
  colour in a status-bar icon and keeps only the alpha channel, so anything with fill detail
  arrives as a solid white blob — which is exactly what the launcher icon does when FCM falls
  back to it, and the reason this file exists. Referenced from AndroidManifest.xml as
  `com.google.firebase.messaging.default_notification_icon`.

  A bell rather than the Grapevine mark: the mark's shape only reads at colour, and reduced
  to one flat alpha it is an unrecognisable lump at 24dp. A bell is legible at that size and
  is what the notification actually means.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">
